        "reasoning": "NBRC361 resolves Neutralized Na2S·9H2O as an operationally prepared stock:1.5g Na2S·9H2O in100mL water, autoclaved121C15min underN2; after cooling, sterile2N H2SO4 is added dropwise to aboutpH7.3 in a sealed vessel. Its0.5g ingredient entry is a dose expressed as starting sulfide, not proof of neat neutralized sodium sulfide. Acid amount/speciation is endpoint-dependent; preserve the preparation rather than minting an exact stoichiometric compound. TOGO-M1560 annotates this row GMO_001601 with label Disodio persulfide nonahydrate and simple/defined properties. That annotation conflicts with the explicit Na2S·9H2O sulfide precursor and does not denote the acid-neutralized preparation; it is retained as source disagreement, not used as chemical identity support. Completeness reassessment: This operational source-qualified stock is defined by explicit precursor amount,water,acidandpHendpoint. It does not assert a stoichiometric neutralizedsulfide compound or exact final dissolvedspeciation. CurrentTOGO Disodiopersulfidenonahydrate annotation remains rejected as identitysupport. A native-validated isolated owner proposal now records this operational stock with its complete source-listed preparation inputs. MIM #1167 successor removes the preparation/storage atmosphere gas from material components while retaining the actual gas condition in source evidence and notes. No gas-solute amount or final dissolved speciation is inferred.",
