        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "JCM722 specifies 3 g Hy-Case Amino (Sigma) in CYS medium. Sigma/Millipore C0501 explicitly calls Hy-Case Amino a bovine-milk casein acid hydrolysate, powder, predominantly free amino acids with some peptides, and reports 25-40% sodium chloride. This supports the branded acid digest product and contradicts equivalence to intact casein, an enzymatic casein digest, or a single amino acid. The recipe has no lot or catalog number, so C0501 is current supplier product corroboration rather than proof of the exact historical lot. Completeness reassessment: Original JCM722 identifies Hy-Case Amino (Sigma), and official C0501 identifies the named bovine-milk casein acid hydrolysate. It is a complex powder of free amino acids, some peptides and salts, distinct from enzymatic N-Z-Amine, intact casein or any single amino acid. Current product identity supports the named product; historical lot quantitative composition is not asserted. An isolated guarded existing-owner promotion now supplies the exact registry identity and supported material scope.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "Applies only to this exact source profile and source_case_id, preserving its raw label and frozen count definition. All admitted recipe contexts and embedded downstream holds are bound by the case evidence. Listed owner records are inspected current candidates; a candidate is approved only to the narrow scope expressly stated in reasoning. Registry correspondence does not approve external chemistry, whole owner records, biological claims or complete SSSOM payloads.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
