        "reasoning": "JCM969 uses 10 g EBIOS dried yeast tablets and footnotes Asahi Food & Healthcare, Tokyo. The current official Asahi EBIOS tablet page confirms dried yeast tablets and lists lactose hydrate, calcium hydrogen phosphate, anhydrous silica and hardened oil as excipients. It does not establish the historical recipe lot formulation, but it demonstrates that the branded tablet is not interchangeable with pure yeast extract or the EBIOS P2G extract discussed in the owner’s old research. The source material here is the tablet preparation. Completeness reassessment: JCM969 explicitly specifies Asahi EBIOS dried-yeast tablets,10g. This source-linked owner denotes the tablet product, not EBIOS P2G yeast extract discussed in historical research. Current official tablet ingredients are evidence for the present product only; the historical source establishes dried-yeast tablet form but not excipient quantities or unchanged composition across time. Bare EBIOS is retained as a rejected unqualified brand label so it cannot globally resolve P2G or other EBIOS products to this tablet owner. An isolated guarded existing-owner promotion now supplies the exact registry identity and supported material scope.",
