        "reasoning": "DSMZ727 uses5g Lab Lemco powder(Oxoid); admitted CCAP C23 andC26 use1g OxoidL29 perlitre, andC27 uses that ingredient in its EG submedium mixed1:1withJM. Current CCAP originals confirm the Lab-Lemco quantities and nesting. The official Oxoid LP0029 specification identifies a refined powder meat-extract product with bounded analytical properties, not a molecular chemical or an arbitrary beef extract. The earlier ThermoL0029B capture is an error wrapper and supplies no scientific support. Completeness reassessment: Oxoid Lab-Lemco is a refined meat-extract powder, identified by original DSMZ727 and CCAP CHM/EG/EG:JM formulations and current official LP0029 specification. This whole variable-composition product is not one molecule or a finished medium. The exact molecular constituent list and historical lot composition are not established and are not required to preserve the named product identity. Current supplier compositional ranges are not backdated to historical lots. An isolated guarded existing-owner promotion now supplies the exact registry identity and supported material scope.",
