        "reasoning": "DSMZ863 fully defines Sodium carbonate solution: dissolve106g Na2CO3 in1litre degassedH2O, then autoclave in sealed serum bottles underCO2; add24ml to the basal medium. This is source-specific formulation evidence, not an unspecified carbonate stock. The current Sodium_Carbonate_Solution owner is typed as a stock but uses neat-compound CHEBI:29377 and carries anhydrous reagent, buffer and malformed aliases. Official CHEBI:29377 describes the dry carbonate formula CO3.2Na, not this prepared solution. The admitted g_l59.7638 is not used as a stock formulation. Completeness reassessment: Original DSMZ863 specifies106g Na2CO3 dissolved in1L degassed water, autoclaved sealed underCO2 and supplied at24mL to the receiving medium. This preparation-qualified stock has its own registry identity. Existing CHEBI29377 stock-labelled owner has1751 historical membership and mixed dry/buffer aliases; this proposal neither repurposes that owner nor moves its counts/aliases. Raw Sodium carbonate solution requires this exact occurrence context and is retained as non-resolving source text on the new owner. A complete isolated new-owner proposal is supplied. MIM #1167 successor removes the preparation/storage atmosphere gas from material components while retaining the actual gas condition in source evidence and notes. No gas-solute amount or final dissolved speciation is inferred.",
