        "reasoning": "The source formula Li2B4O7 identifies the nominal bulk lithium tetraborate material. DSMZ/MediaDive preserve that formula; the primary Sigma222534 product identifies lithium tetraborate with CAS12007-60-2 and B4Li2O7. The proposed CAS assignment is a curation inference at that bulk-material scope, with a broad relation to verified CHEBI:190479 inorganic lithium salt. Exact ChEBI searches found no matching term; CHEBI:38910 has incompatible lithium:boron stoichiometry, and CHEBI:38889 is the hydroxylated H4B4O9 anion. The coordinator cache preserves two B4Li2O7 PubChem records with different connectivity (CIDs15764247 and9815330); neither structure is selected or treated as interchangeable. CID21895667 has incompatible B4Li12O12, while CID90478374 is an explicit pentahydrate and is not assigned. The exact CAS-name query returns9815330, but this is a database lookup rather than independent CAS certification or proof of the source reagent. No vendor, lot, hydration assay, polymorph, CID, InChI or SMILES is asserted by the proposal.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "Individually reviewed source case 159: 'Li2B4O7'; all 2 original occurrence IDs and full frozen recipe contexts are retained in RS-159-FROZEN. Primary references are scoped to those exact recipes or explicitly identified chemical/product candidates; no identity or concentration is transferred to a different preparation. This review preserves every inherited source/native hold and does not approve roles or release.",
