        "reasoning": "Both NBRC1020 and824 explicitly define resazurin1 g pluswater1 L, added1 ml. This source agreement supports a common recipe context across the two occurrences. It does not establish resazurin sodium salt, and a neat-resazurin MIM record cannot represent the entire stock prepared with1g reagent and1L added water. Current exact proposal basis: Literal printed masses and added distilled-water volume per source preparation. G/MG_PER_PREPARATION_WITH_1_L_WATER describes a recipe batch containing1L added water, not a final1L solution or final concentration. The full named source preparation is scientifically identified. Raw local names and bare numbered pointers are preserved as REJECTED_LABEL, not global resolver aliases; each original occurrence receives only its explicit source-qualified assignment. Component grounding, variable titrant amounts and unrelated release assertions retain their stated boundaries.",
