        "reasoning": "The frozen source and TOGO M2816 identify EZMix-N-Z-amineA in S.islandicus DT medium, with raw0.1(w/v) notation. Official SigmaC4464 identifies the named product as an enzymatic casein hydrolysate from bovine milk. It is distinct from acid-hydrolyzed Hy-CaseAmino(case171), intact casein or a single amino acid. The likely primary paperPMC3754178 was located, but direct fulltextAPI,PMC and publisher retrievals failed or returned browser-check pages; its fulltext was not independently inspected here. The unit notation must therefore be preserved without silently converting it to0.1g/L. The official Sigma C4464 product capture identifies EZMix N-Z-Amine A as an enzymatic bovine-milk casein hydrolysate. This is a named complex product, not acid Hy-Case or pure casein. The existing generic N-Z-Amine A owner is a potential product-line parent/merge candidate but its source2439 does not establish identical EZMix supplied preparation; no merge is proposed. Historical DT-medium amount/percentage remains a separate source-dose question; it is not an identity blocker for this named product. No ingredient proportions, nutritional roles or unverified whole-protein components are asserted.",
