        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "TOGO M134, M1620 and M838 specify100mL filtered tomato juice in their corresponding recipes; current JCM143 and NBRC820 corroborate their recipe rows. The current JCM803 endpoint returns Nothing found, so its original-source content is not independently confirmed here. Filtering is a preparation qualifier of a complex biological liquid, not whole tomato tissue or a chemically defined solute. Frozen100G_PER_L in each occurrence contradicts the capturedTOGO mL amounts. The10% recipe title does not authorize a chemical identity or mass conversion. Official MicrO defines tomato juice obtained by maceration followed by filtration. This exact preparation category matches the original JCM143/NBRC820/NBRC1271 wording. The frozen JCM803-derived occurrence is supported by TOGO only because current JCM803 returns Nothing found; that limitation is retained. No cultivar, fraction composition, nutritional role, pH7 pretreatment or final-medium dose is added to the identity.",
