        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "TOGO M2935 specifies Oxoid SR0117 Campylobacter selective supplement alongside Columbia agar base CM0331 and 5% sheep blood. The catalogue identifier denotes a formulated supplement, not one antibiotic, blood or the complete Skirrow medium. The source provides no dose, so a modern vial recommendation cannot supply its concentration. TOGO M2935 identifies Oxoid SR0117 separately from Columbia agar base and blood. The current official SR0117E page identifies Preston Campylobacter Selective Supplement, freeze-dried. This establishes the product family; current500mL-per-vial guidance is not an observed historical recipe dose. The source does not supply a historical formulation revision or dose, so no components, amounts or antibiotic-specific mechanisms are guessed. The product identity is supported independently of those missing quantitative details.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "Individually reviewed source case 51: 'Campylobacter selective supplement (Oxoid SR0117)'; all 1 original occurrence IDs and full frozen recipe contexts are retained in RS-051-FROZEN. Primary references are scoped to those exact recipes or explicitly identified chemical/product candidates; no identity or concentration is transferred to a different preparation. This review preserves every inherited source/native hold and does not approve roles or release.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
    "scope_note": "Binding original complete-payload scientific assessments plus actual immutable successor reviews; source-case acceptance alone is not used as owner approval. Historical open findings remain superseded only by separately bound actual corrections."
