        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "The four TOGO source tables explicitly qualify AlK(SO4)2 as anhydrous, including ATCC1191 mineral elixir and ATCC trace-mineral supplement contexts. OLS CHEBI:86463 has Al.K.2O4S with no waters and is the existing owner identity. This supports an anhydrous alias, while the twelve-water record remains separate.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "All 4 original occurrences were reviewed in their complete frozen recipe contexts. Evidence applies to the exact preserved source label 'AlK(SO4)2 (anhydrous)'; source component, stock, salt, hydration and charge scopes are interpreted only as stated in the case reasoning. No inherited hold or downstream identity authorization is removed. Source-unit discrepancy: TOGO M3174 Wolfe mineral elixir gives anhydrous alum10mg, while its frozen flattened occurrence records10G_PER_L; the other ATCC-trace-supplement occurrences preserve0.01g. This alias/owner proposal makes no unit conversion or receiving-medium concentration approval.",
        "source_observations": null
      },
