        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "The four JCM media1030-1033 and MediaDive solution5083 explicitly supply CrK(SO4)2·12H2O. The formula is the potassium/chromium(III) double sulfate dodecahydrate, corroborated by the supplier chrome-alum record CAS7788-99-0. Existing CrKSO42_X_12_H2O has that CAS identity. Add the correctly parenthesized source spelling without collapsing the double salt into chromium(III) sulfate. The original JCM1033 HTML attempt returned Nothing found; the separately captured complete bacmedia JCM1033 PDF corroborates the trace-element spelling. This later recovery does not change the old capture classification or approve receiving-medium quantities. The separately captured TOGO and MediaDive solution5083 records specify CrK(SO4)2·12H2O in the source contexts. The retained JCM1033 route returns Nothing found and is not positive original recipe evidence. Supplier identity/CAS7788-99-0 corroborates potassium chromium double sulfate dodecahydrate. NLM exact narrower concept M0314280 supplies the form-specific identity; the old CHEBI53471 relationship is superseded because its Cr2(SO4)3 formula differs in potassium and sulfate ratio as well as water.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "All 5 original occurrences were reviewed in their complete frozen recipe contexts. Evidence applies to the exact preserved source label 'CrK(SO4)2 x 12 H2O'; source component, stock, salt, hydration and charge scopes are interpreted only as stated in the case reasoning. No inherited hold or downstream identity authorization is removed. Successor #1241 evidence-status correction: failed captures are retained as unsuccessful searches, and ontology captures are distinguished from original recipes. Their raw bytes and access times are unchanged. All 5 original occurrences were reviewed in their complete frozen recipe contexts. Evidence applies to the exact preserved source label 'CrK(SO4)2 x 12 H2O'; source component, stock, salt, hydration and charge scopes are interpreted only as stated in the case reasoning. No inherited hold or downstream identity authorization is removed. Positive source support excludes the failed JCM1033 response. Exact form mapping does not authorize any source quantity normalization.",
        "source_observations": null
      },
      {
        "worker_slot": 2,
        "binding": {
          "path": "/Users/marcin/Documents/VIMSS/ontology/Mechs/MediaIngredientMech/.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/integration/final-campaign-planning-v1/observed-inputs-v1/snapshot/w02/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-02/seven-preparation-types-v1/selected-v3/decisions.json",
