        "reasoning": "TOGO M2760 explicitly names and types magnesium sulfate dihydrate (GMO_002282). Supplier Parchem identifies CAS17830-05-6 and H4MgO6S; the PubChem structure has two waters. The bounded OLS search returned no exact dihydrate term, while CHEBI:32599 is the anhydrous parent. Propose a distinct CAS identity with NARROW_MATCH grounding to the parent; the monohydrate and heptahydrate owners are not equivalent. Primary NLM D008278 concept review additionally found generic sulfate and heptahydrate only, without a dihydrate concept in that record. This bounded search does not assert absence from all ontologies.",
