        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "JCM1030-1033 and MediaDive solution5083 explicitly list SrSO4 in the trace-element recipe, with Togo GMO002069 naming strontium sulfate. Live OLS CHEBI:747199 is nonobsolete and has formula Sr.O4S, CAS7759-02-6 and the corresponding strontium(2+) sulfate structure. This supports a new distinct strontium sulfate ingredient; none of the strontium chloride owners is equivalent. The original JCM1033 HTML attempt returned Nothing found; the separately captured complete bacmedia JCM1033 PDF corroborates the trace-element spelling. This later recovery does not change the old capture classification or approve receiving-medium quantities.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "All 6 original occurrences were reviewed in their complete frozen recipe contexts. Evidence applies to the exact preserved source label 'SrSO4'; source component, stock, salt, hydration and charge scopes are interpreted only as stated in the case reasoning. No inherited hold or downstream identity authorization is removed. Source-unit discrepancy: TOGO M1094 trace solution gives SrSO4 as0.92mg, while its frozen flattened occurrence records0.92G_PER_L. Independent MediaDive5083 explicitly records0.00092g/L within the trace solution. This identity proposal approves no receiving-medium concentration and does not erase the conflicting source occurrence. Successor #1241 evidence-status correction: failed captures are retained as unsuccessful searches, and ontology captures are distinguished from original recipes. Their raw bytes and access times are unchanged.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
