        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "The DSMZ375 original explicitly administers cysteine from a sterile anoxic stock prepared under 100% N2; its 0.30 g table amount is receiving solute, not stock concentration. The three375 occurrences therefore receive a bounded unspecified-strength preparation proposal. The three1107 occurrences keep their explicit 5% w/v preparation. Intended two-water form/stereochemistry remain unresolved; filtration of DTT/vitamins in375 does not establish cysteine filtration. The two scopes may overlap, with neither full equivalence nor chemical distinctness asserted.",
        "missing_requirement": "For exact chemical identity or overlap closure, establish the intended cysteine hydrate/stereochemistry and375 stock strength, carrier and sterilization method. These are unknown fields, not a blocker to the bounded source-named preparation.",
        "applicability": "Final-correction successor for this exact frozen case digest, raw source object and all original occurrence IDs. Every original occurrence is bound individually in source-occurrence-bindings.json; unchanged case58 contexts are identified as inherited rather than newly reviewed. All existing nonpositive decisions, source/version/quantity and cross-shard obligations remain. This is author-stage scientific curation, not final owner/export approval; new independent final-byte review is pending.",
