        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "DSMZ280 supplies trimethylamine-HCl; CHEBI64700 is equimolar trimethylamine hydrochloride. The multiplication separator in Trimethylamine x HCl denotes the same salt. Existing Methylamine-HCl EXACT_SYNONYM is a different one-carbon amine salt (CHEBI59337/CAS593-51-1), not three-carbon trimethylamine hydrochloride (CAS593-81-7); preserve but reject the wrong alias.",
        "missing_requirement": "Historical SEM:069f2686d478755f354c and prior merged Methylamine owner require coordinator reconciliation; proposed rejection does not restore lost source attribution automatically.",
        "applicability": "Case index 100: all 1 original occurrences and complete frozen recipe snapshots were read. DSMZ280 supplies trimethylamine-HCl; CHEBI64700 is equimolar trimethylamine hydrochloride. The multiplication separator in Trimethylamine x HCl denotes the same salt. Existing Methylamine-HCl EXACT_SYNONYM is a different one-carbon amine salt (CHEBI59337/CAS593-51-1), not three-carbon trimethylamine hydrochloride (CAS593-81-7); preserve but reject the wrong alias. Evidence from another recipe or manufacturer is used only for the stated chemical/form comparison, never to replace missing source recipe context. All frozen downstream/native holds remain in force.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
