        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "The frozen raw formula Ce(NO3)3 x6H2O and live ingredient1587 CAS10294-41-4 agree. Independent Sigma238538 and PubChem16211466 explicitly establish cerium(III) nitrate hexahydrate and six waters, resolving the old formula/CAS gap. The proposal preserves the flattened source text, adds the original parenthesized spelling, and uses cas:10294-41-4 with the closest broader MeSH cerium(III) nitrate concept M0319657. OLS finds an exact SNOMED substance term725783009, but SNOMED is not a permitted OntologySourceEnum in this frozen schema; no exact eligible term was found in the captured CHEBI/all-OLS name/CAS queries. NLM distinguishes narrower Ce(III) concept M0319657, CAS10108-73-3, from the descriptor including Ce(IV); the Ce(III) concept is the closer form-of parent. It is not exact hexahydrate identity. The flattened producer label CeNO33 x 6 H2O is retained with its original provenance as non-resolving REJECTED_LABEL, because loss of parentheses changes literal formula stoichiometry; only the verified provider spelling is a resolving source alias.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "Assessment applies only to mediadive mediadive.ingredient:1587 and frozen raw record {\"amount\": 0.06, \"compound\": \"Ce(NO3)3 x 6 H2O\", \"compound_id\": 1587, \"g_l\": 0.06, \"optional\": 0, \"recipe_order\": 10, \"unit\": \"g\"}. Frozen occurrences=1 has definition 'helper constant; not measured recipe frequency'; it is not reinterpreted as recipe frequency. Live ingredient/recipe records are explicit primary comparisons, not replacements for the frozen input. All existing WITHHOLD, REJECTED_LABEL and source-material obligations remain; no complete owner or export approval is inferred.",
