        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "The original La(NO3)3 x6H2O, MediaDive1586 CAS10277-43-7, Sigma331937 and PubChem exact six-water identity agree on lanthanum(III) nitrate hexahydrate. Official NLM browser explicitly assigns CAS10277-43-7 to narrower MeSH concept M0313204, labelled lanthanide nitrate hexahydrate, under the descriptor whose synonyms include lanthanum nitrate. The exact concept preserves the six-water scope that the broader descriptor C016534 would lose. The production local adapter independently resolves the M concept canonical label; the proposal therefore uses mesh:M0313204 with CAS_RN_LOOKUP provenance and retains the CAS/form evidence. An OLS search returning only descriptor classes was insufficient to establish absence of this exact concept. The flattened producer label LaNO33 x 6 H2O is retained with its original provenance as non-resolving REJECTED_LABEL, because loss of parentheses changes literal formula stoichiometry; only the verified provider spelling is a resolving source alias.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "Assessment applies only to mediadive mediadive.ingredient:1586 and frozen raw record {\"amount\": 0.06, \"compound\": \"La(NO3)3 x 6 H2O\", \"compound_id\": 1586, \"g_l\": 0.06, \"optional\": 0, \"recipe_order\": 9, \"unit\": \"g\"}. Frozen occurrences=1 has definition 'helper constant; not measured recipe frequency'; it is not reinterpreted as recipe frequency. Live ingredient/recipe records are explicit primary comparisons, not replacements for the frozen input. All existing WITHHOLD, REJECTED_LABEL and source-material obligations remain; no complete owner or export approval is inferred.",
        "source_observations": null
