        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "DSMZ1555 explicitly names MPBiomedical lipoprotein concentrate as an LPC supplement. The 0.1% is its receiving-medium dose. The existing placeholder can therefore represent this manufacturer-associated, source-qualified concentrate now; current MPBio catalogue composition is not imposed on the older recipe. The unqualified raw label is retained non-resolving on the qualified owner to avoid product-family equivalence.",
        "missing_requirement": "No missing fact blocks this source-qualified named material. Catalogue/version, cholesterol concentration and biological origin remain unspecified fields, not reasons to postpone identity representation.",
        "applicability": "Issue1201 continuation of this exact frozen source case. DSMZ1555 explicitly names MPBiomedical lipoprotein concentrate as an LPC supplement. The 0.1% is its receiving-medium dose. The existing placeholder can therefore represent this manufacturer-associated, source-qualified concentrate now; current MPBio catalogue composition is not imposed on the older recipe. The unqualified raw label is retained non-resolving on the qualified owner to avoid product-family equivalence. Helper/incident-edge count definitions, original source ID and raw label are unchanged. Every inherited nonpositive row decision, source placeholder and downstream hold remains in force. Scope-specific proposals do not approve generic labels globally or release complete owner/export payloads.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
