        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "MediaDive1763 names Mg(NO3)2 x6H2O with CAS13446-18-9, independently corroborated by PubChem; the existing hexahydrate owner already has that distinct CAS and broader nitrate parent. Full payload inspection additionally found flattened MgNO32 x6H2O as resolving RAW_TEXT. The proposal preserves that malformed spelling as REJECTED_LABEL, retaining the correct parenthesized source alias and all previous mapping history.",
        "missing_requirement": "None for the known hexahydrate identity. The concrete malformed-token correction is proposed; no complete-owner or export hold is cleared.",
        "applicability": "Issue1201 continuation of this exact frozen source case. MediaDive1763 names Mg(NO3)2 x6H2O with CAS13446-18-9, independently corroborated by PubChem; the existing hexahydrate owner already has that distinct CAS and broader nitrate parent. Full payload inspection additionally found flattened MgNO32 x6H2O as resolving RAW_TEXT. The proposal preserves that malformed spelling as REJECTED_LABEL, retaining the correct parenthesized source alias and all previous mapping history. Helper/incident-edge count definitions, original source ID and raw label are unchanged. Every inherited nonpositive row decision, source placeholder and downstream hold remains in force. Scope-specific proposals do not approve generic labels globally or release complete owner/export payloads.",
        "source_observations": null
