        "reasoning": "The explicit six-water magnesium-sulfate source matches the existing local hexahydrate owner. Primary American Elements datasheet and independent EPA2020-14401/ILO-WHO ICSC1197 identify hexahydrate CAS17830-18-1. A specific verified registry identifier is available, so the proposal replaces the local primary while preserving the asymmetric CHEBI32599 parent, existing formula and all rejected wrong-hydrate labels. No supplier melting point or anhydrous properties are copied.",
        "missing_requirement": "None for the source-stated hexahydrate and independently verified CAS; source anhydrous annotations remain a separate correction obligation.",
        "applicability": "Issue1201 continuation of this exact frozen source case. The explicit six-water magnesium-sulfate source matches the existing local hexahydrate owner. Primary American Elements datasheet and independent EPA2020-14401/ILO-WHO ICSC1197 identify hexahydrate CAS17830-18-1. A specific verified registry identifier is available, so the proposal replaces the local primary while preserving the asymmetric CHEBI32599 parent, existing formula and all rejected wrong-hydrate labels. No supplier melting point or anhydrous properties are copied. Helper/incident-edge count definitions, original source ID and raw label are unchanged. Every inherited nonpositive row decision, source placeholder and downstream hold remains in force. Scope-specific proposals do not approve generic labels globally or release complete owner/export payloads.",
