        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "JCM616 and MediaDive J616 both actually print MnCl4 x4H2O. The existing manganese(II)-chloride tetrahydrate owner contains two chlorides, so dropping the extra two chlorides would change the literal chemistry. Expanded lookup found chloride dihydrate, tetrahydrate and anhydrous owners but no evidence correcting the four-chloride reagent. A local formula-shaped node would not cure the source conflict.",
        "missing_requirement": "The manganese oxidation/chloride stoichiometry intended by the original recipe must be established by an author correction or reagent specification; a lexical MnCl4→MnCl2 repair is not evidence.",
        "applicability": "Issue1201 continuation of this exact frozen source case. JCM616 and MediaDive J616 both actually print MnCl4 x4H2O. The existing manganese(II)-chloride tetrahydrate owner contains two chlorides, so dropping the extra two chlorides would change the literal chemistry. Expanded lookup found chloride dihydrate, tetrahydrate and anhydrous owners but no evidence correcting the four-chloride reagent. A local formula-shaped node would not cure the source conflict. Helper/incident-edge count definitions, original source ID and raw label are unchanged. Every inherited nonpositive row decision, source placeholder and downstream hold remains in force. Scope-specific proposals do not approve generic labels globally or release complete owner/export payloads.",
