        "reasoning": "TOGO M2716 trace-elements table explicitly types Fe(SO4)2(NH4)2·6H2O as ammonium iron(II) sulfate hexahydrate. Rearranging the two ammonium and two sulfate groups changes no stoichiometry; six waters remain explicit. CHEBI:76181 confirms this hydrate, and the existing Mohr-salt hexahydrate owner is the appropriate identity.",
