        "reasoning": "Both TOGO M1094/JCM1030 and M940/JCM899 identify (NH4)2Fe(SO4)2·6H2O as ammonium iron(II) sulfate hexahydrate. OLS CHEBI:76181 verifies that exact six-water double salt. The group-order variant adds no chloride or other component and is a safe alias for the existing hydrate owner.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "All 2 original occurrences were reviewed in their complete frozen recipe contexts. Evidence applies to the exact preserved source label '(NH4)2Fe(SO4)2·6H2O'; source component, stock, salt, hydration and charge scopes are interpreted only as stated in the case reasoning. No inherited hold or downstream identity authorization is removed. Source-unit discrepancies: TOGO M1094 trace solution gives Mohr salt78.4mg and M940 gives784mg, while frozen flattened occurrences retain those numeric values asG_PER_L. This identity/alias proposal approves neither unit normalization nor receiving-medium concentration.",
        "source_observations": null
