        "reasoning": "The frozen TOGO M3164 ingredient explicitly gives Fe(SO4)2(NH4)2·6H2O. Its group order is algebraically identical to Fe(NH4)2(SO4)2·6H2O, corroborated by CHEBI:76181 and the primary TOGO M2716 equivalent written with a spaced dot. It contains no extra chloride and preserves six waters; add it to the existing Mohr-salt hydrate owner.",
