        "applicability": "Issue1201 continuation of this exact frozen source case. MediaDive106 independently attaches CAS7783-85-9 and a six-water formula to its bare Fe(NH4)2(SO4)2 name, supporting the existing Mohr-hexahydrate interpretation at this source. Expanded lookup also finds the anhydrous and seven-water owners, so bare text is not treated as a universal hydrate alias. Full owner inspection found three concentration-qualified stock tokens incorrectly accepted as hydrate synonyms; the complete selected successor preserves those stock tokens as REJECTED_LABEL and also retires the two underqualified global aliases. Supported occurrence-specific CAS/form reasoning remains distinct from global resolver scope. Helper/incident-edge count definitions, original source ID and raw label are unchanged. Every inherited nonpositive row decision, source placeholder and downstream hold remains in force. Scope-specific proposals do not approve generic labels globally or release complete owner/export payloads.",
