        },
        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "The complete Togo M2596 source defines SS from Ithaca wastewater digester sludge: sequential centrifugation, pH7 adjustment with1M HCl,0.8µm prefiltration, nitrogen purge and0.8–0.2µm sterile filtration. It explicitly adds25%(v/v) SS. Sludge fluid in the frozen flattened recipe is a nested preparation input, not a separate basal supplement. The source does not add yeast extract during SS preparation; DSMZ119 yeast-treated sludge fluid is a different product. Propose this source-defined processed material without representing sludge/HCl extraction inputs as final molecular components.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "Applies to exact culturemech source case 'Anaerobic digestor sludge supernatant (SS)', raw label 'Anaerobic digestor sludge supernatant (SS)'. All 1 frozen occurrences were read, including full recipe context; the source IDs, doses, nested stock paths and preparation qualifiers remain in the bound input and occurrence assessment. The complete Togo M2596 source defines SS from Ithaca wastewater digester sludge: sequential centrifugation, pH7 adjustment with1M HCl,0.8µm prefiltration, nitrogen purge and0.8–0.2µm sterile filtration. It explicitly adds25%(v/v) SS. Sludge fluid in the frozen flattened recipe is a nested preparation input, not a separate basal supplement. The source does not add yeast extract during SS preparation; DSMZ119 yeast-treated sludge fluid is a different product. Propose this source-defined processed material without representing sludge/HCl extraction inputs as final molecular components. Current primary Togo API recipe inspected where referenced; raw names outrank inferred GMO annotations and nested preparation structure is retained.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
