        },
        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "Primary Sitrin et al.1985 isolated aridicins A/B/C separately by preparative HPLC and characterized B (Table1 empirical formula C82H84N8O30Cl4). Chung et al.1986 printed652 explicitly states aridicin was renamed ardacin, and Figure1 distinguishes the B factor. The existing kgmicrobe.compound:ardacin_b owner can therefore represent this distinct factor with an asymmetric glycopeptide-class parent CHEBI:24396. This is not an exact or broader relation to generic NCIT:C169786 or CHEBI:753252 ardacin complex; those terms lack an independently inspected factor-B definition. No supplier, pure preparation, CAS or reconstructed stereostructure is invented.",
        "missing_requirement": "The exact relationship of the generic Ardacin ontology concepts to factor B and any supplied commercial preparation/purity remain unverified. These do not prevent a bounded distinct-factor representation.",
        "applicability": "Applies only to frozen case KG_CASE:50d0de269a2e55b7187caeb239d2e01a0ab7b42438853727b94e1d05700e6a5b, source metatraits, identifier kgmicrobe.compound:ardacin_b; every listed recipe context and exact raw/processed label remains bound by case_input_sha256. KG helper/graph occurrence definition is retained verbatim and is not asserted to be recipe frequency. Matching lexical labels do not extend source identity to unrelated cases. All inherited downstream and complete-payload publication holds remain in force.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
