        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "The raw source(NH4)6Mo7O24 x4H2O, ingredient120 CAS12054-85-2 and mass1235.86 identify hexaammonium heptamolybdate tetrahydrate86244. Diammonium orthomolybdate91249 has one Mo and two ammoniums and is not its parent. The current wrong owner already rejects the tetrahydrate strings but still resolves the anhydrous heptamolybdate formula; reject that residual polyanion alias and link the source to the existing correct tetrahydrate owner. OLS86244's prose says heptahydrate in error; its name/formula/mass and source CAS all specify four waters.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "Applies only to frozen case KG_CASE:2b3d618b22b4ea8fe5e1e90bbe262449f99b21b7fbf96288f9427d7e75640c4f, source mediadive, identifier mediadive.ingredient:120; every listed recipe context and exact raw/processed label remains bound by case_input_sha256. KG helper/graph occurrence definition is retained verbatim and is not asserted to be recipe frequency. Matching lexical labels do not extend source identity to unrelated cases. All inherited downstream and complete-payload publication holds remain in force.",
