        "reasoning": "Exact provenance binds MediaDive1188 to DSMZ1344 Taps 17.4 g. The original recipe and manufacturer T5130/108320 nomenclature establish the conventional TAPS buffer name, N-[tris(hydroxymethyl)methyl]-3-aminopropanesulfonic acid (CHEBI:191055, CAS29915-38-6). Represent that free-buffer identity separately from CAS91000-53-2 sodium salt and from the automatically matched Tyr-Arg-Phe-Sar peptide. No Sigma purchase, lot assay or sodium salt is inferred from pH8.3. The existing sodium-salt alias rejection remains valid. Method correction only: the new explicit unique CAS29915-38-6 lookup in hash-bound CHEBI255 resolves to the unchanged191055 target; CAS_RN_LOOKUP replaces the unsupported ontology-synonym claim. The original supplier/systematic-name/source1188 identity evidence and every hold remain.",
