          "row_sha256": "27df785cd95a299028f51d5909593afc50ac8c7a8c69170ce7b8c92f096200ad"
        },
        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "All seven occurrences denote filtered natural seawater as an input before mixing or autoclaving. CCAP MErds/NSS low require filling to one litre with it; MY75S and ZM10 explicitly dilute that input. NSS low and 2SNA allow synthetic salt alternatives, which remain separate alternatives. This scoped input is consistent with the Filtered Seawater owner; final-medium dilution and autoclaving do not turn its input label into a different source ingredient. Final-review qualification of the historical #260 dilution rationale: the original CCAP PE footnote explicitly says to filter natural seawater, reduce it to 95% using glass distilled water, and autoclave. That prepared input is then dosed at 950 cm3; the prior dilution is not inferred from the receiving-medium dose. The literal 95%-strength label is retained as REJECTED_LABEL on this bare filtered-seawater owner, without inventing the percentage basis, final volume, component ratio or a new preparation owner. The unqualified Natural seawater alias is also nonresolving: its recovered JCM1377 contexts state natural seawater without filtration. Supported Filtered natural seawater and Natural seawater (filtrated) aliases remain. Earlier #260 mapping evidence and histories are preserved as historical rationale, superseded only on these alias applicability points by this source-backed qualification. The two assigned filtered cases are not reinterpreted as the 95% preparation. Sources: https://www.ccap.ac.uk/wp-content/uploads/MR_PE.pdf ; https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1377 .",
        "missing_requirement": "The full existing Filtered_Seawater payload, especially its unqualified Natural seawater alias, still requires independent publication review after any alias edit.",
        "applicability": "Applies only to culturemech Filtered natural seawater (raw label 'Filtered natural seawater'). All 7 occurrence components and full frozen recipe snapshots were read, including preparation and nested solutions: CultureMech:000089 ingredients/0, CultureMech:000095 ingredients/3, CultureMech:000107 ingredients/1, CultureMech:000146 ingredients/17, CultureMech:000411 ingredients/2, CultureMech:000364 ingredients/0, CultureMech:000383 ingredients/1.",
        "source_observations": null
      },
      {
        "worker_slot": 4,
        "binding": {
          "path": "/Users/marcin/Documents/VIMSS/ontology/Mechs/MediaIngredientMech/.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/integration/final-campaign-planning-v1/observed-inputs-v1/snapshot/w04/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-04/successors/taps-method-v1/decisions.json",
          "sha256": "64fa1b4a11cbb20c261bb40018d507267bfc388d6993dce652adebd46572b57a",
          "selector": "/69",
          "row_sha256": "9e2083a7882fbf591f0a731c6d1a29f1ecb24b7afd2ab5c35e16cb320ed6aca3"
        },
        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "JCM1102 explicitly lists 750 ml Natural seawater (filtrated) as an input alongside 250 ml distilled water; all four frozen TOGO variants preserve that same input while varying supplements. Filtrated and filtered name the same treatment here. The identity candidate is the existing Filtered Seawater material, not the complete anaerobic medium or its 75% dilution. Final-review qualification of the historical #260 dilution rationale: the original CCAP PE footnote explicitly says to filter natural seawater, reduce it to 95% using glass distilled water, and autoclave. That prepared input is then dosed at 950 cm3; the prior dilution is not inferred from the receiving-medium dose. The literal 95%-strength label is retained as REJECTED_LABEL on this bare filtered-seawater owner, without inventing the percentage basis, final volume, component ratio or a new preparation owner. The unqualified Natural seawater alias is also nonresolving: its recovered JCM1377 contexts state natural seawater without filtration. Supported Filtered natural seawater and Natural seawater (filtrated) aliases remain. Earlier #260 mapping evidence and histories are preserved as historical rationale, superseded only on these alias applicability points by this source-backed qualification. The two assigned filtered cases are not reinterpreted as the 95% preparation. Sources: https://www.ccap.ac.uk/wp-content/uploads/MR_PE.pdf ; https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1377 .",
        "missing_requirement": "The edited owner requires new content-bound publication review; this case does not settle its unrelated existing alias scope or release holds.",
        "applicability": "Applies only to culturemech Natural seawater (filtrated) (raw label 'Natural seawater (filtrated)'). All 4 occurrence components and full frozen recipe snapshots were read, including preparation and nested solutions: CultureMech:007701 ingredients/3, CultureMech:007702 ingredients/2, CultureMech:007703 ingredients/3, CultureMech:007700 ingredients/3.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
