        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "MediaDive ingredient2112 usage points to DSMZ438, whose original title identifies DIFCO and specifies Bordet-Gengou-Agar-Base before15% horse blood. The KG entry measures1000ml prepared base, so this source-qualified prepared-medium owner is distinct from the predecessor Difco dry-base product. The dry base is an identified material input; hydration quantity/final formulation are unknown and not invented. Historical generic and BD248200 aliases on the old imported2112 owner are retained as provenance, not asserted as exact identities to this ready base. No sheep-blood recipe111 is joined to this horse-blood source. Raw source labels and optional/use instructions are retained in source-case evidence, not installed as global resolving aliases. Existing source/owner/export holds remain; no maintained or release approval. Prior labels and curation provenance: [{\"synonym_text\": \"Bordet-Gengou-Agar-Base\", \"synonym_type\": \"RAW_TEXT\", \"source\": \"mim-queue\"}, {\"synonym_text\": \"Bordet-Gengou Agar Base (BD 248200)\", \"synonym_type\": \"CATALOG_VARIANT\", \"source\": \"culturemech:output/ingredient_occurrences.tsv\"}]. These historical source labels are retained here; no generic label is asserted as an exact source formulation synonym.",
