        "reasoning": "Comparative source annotation only: TOGO M2850 (worker04 case111, not DSMZ111) explicitly gives1L prepared Bordet-Gengou basal agar and a separate15% sheep-blood addition. It supplies no basal formula or vendor. DSMZ438 and ingredient2112 independently identify a Difco prepared basal medium with separate15% horse blood. These contexts establish the basal-versus-supplement boundary, but do not establish whether the two basal preparations have identical formulations or procurement identities. M2850 is not resolved to this Difco438 owner, no M2850 alias or recipe-equivalence is added, and the1L figure is the receiving recipe quantity, not an invented water component. The existing Difco438 identity and its partial component assertion remain unchanged. A source formula or product specification for M2850 that permits comparison with the Difco preparation is the remaining exact-identity fact.",
