        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "Primary Sashihara2000 PMID11193411 and the2001 JGAM reidentification paper establish that the formerly reported Pediococcus sp.ISK-1 was reidentified as Staphylococcus warneri ISK-1. Thus producer-name conflict is not a valid reason by itself to separate the named bacteriocins. However live CHEBI:204272 labels Nukacin ISK-1 while giving a1178.444Da short-peptide structure,which does not establish the reported mature27-residue lantibiotic.",
        "missing_requirement": "Trace this metatraits observation to the original ISK-1 peptide/assay provenance and resolve the CHEBI204272 structure-versus-mature-peptide discrepancy before asserting exact identity.",
