        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "The frozen KJ row has50µl and attribute1mg/ml,so its supplied context is a stock addition. KJ may be historical potassium-iodide notation,but live MediaDive1042 assigns phencyclidine CAS77-10-1/formulaC17H25N,an explicit automated-identifier conflict. Final correction: DSMZ 792b explicitly doses 0.50 ml KI (0.01% w/v) into solution A. This is an aliquoted supplied stock, not neat potassium iodide CHEBI:8346. Mark only this stock label REJECTED_LABEL on the chemical owner, preserving its raw text, source and history. Do not infer stock solvent or use this to settle the separate ambiguous KJ source case.",
        "missing_requirement": "OriginalDSMZ1155 retainsKJ1mg/ml50microlitre withoutspellingoutsolute orsolvent. The full primary1727comparison and providersearch do not establish exactreagentidentity. ProviderCAS77-10-1 isphencyclidinecontamination. Minting an undefinedKJstock would merely rename unresolvedidentity; need authoritativeKJexpansion andsolvent.",
        "applicability": "Existing Ki CHEBI:8346 is a candidate solute owner only. The source stock cannot be equated to pure KI or phencyclidine from these identifiers. Preserve exact volume/strength,with no counterion or solvent invention.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
