        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "The MediaDive77 source explicitly names thiamine hydrochloride dihydrate; OLSCHEBI:132751 independently preserves that exact two-water form. This is distinct from monohydrate cases28/117 and from unhydrated49105. Final correction: Withdraw the active CAS 13465-05-9 and its CAS-retrieval metadata. The direct PubChem name query resolves it to CID 21899424, formula ClH5O2 and InChI=1S/ClH.2H2O/h1H;2*1H2, which lacks the thiamine skeleton. No replacement CAS is established or inserted. Preserve CHEBI:132751, the dihydrate formula/structure, all original history, source labels and WITHHOLD obligations. This repairs the documented false CAS claim under #268 without granting whole-owner or export approval.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "The frozen5mg row with0.005g/L belongs to the dihydrate supplied form already owned by Thiamine-hcl_X_2_H2o. No new alias is required; inherited row/payload holds remain until their separate concerns are resolved.",
