        "reasoning": "Both source records reference ATCC1490 modified chopped meat base; M2574 adds carbohydrates/rumen fluid and M2618 adds formate/fumarate. Base1490 includes processed meat and filtrate, peptone, yeast extract, salts, hemin and vitaminK1 preparations. It is not food meat or Robertson medium.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "TOGO M2574 and M2618 both explicitly list 20 g agar in the ATCC1490 base expansion. The current ATCC1490 PDF presents agar as optional. This candidate denotes the agar-containing branch actually asserted by those two TOGO sources, not the broth branch or every medium called ATCC1490. Added carbohydrates/rumen fluid in M2574 and formate/fumarate in M2618 remain outside this common base. Any conflicting frozen physical-state annotation remains an upstream hold.",
