        "reasoning": "DSMZ87a modifies medium87 by adding vitamin solution CA. Medium87 is the basal whole recipe, while the vitamin solution and its hydrated thiamine ingredient are separate preparations.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "Current DSMZ87 explicitly specifies 1 ml neutralized sulfide solution per 90 ml medium and 0.03% final concentration, with its own stock prepared from 3 g Na2S·9H2O and 100 ml water. MICRO:0001830 quotes the historical 0.015% final concentration and refers to DSMZ27. Other basal quantities agree, but full formulation equivalence is not established. Use a source-qualified registry for the captured current DSMZ87 preparation; no exact or broad mapping to the historical numbered term is proposed.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
