        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "The KOMODO variant explicitly replaces clarified rumen fluid with sludge fluid from medium119. DSMZ119 prepares anaerobic-digester sludge with yeast extract, incubates, centrifuges and retains the clear supernatant. This is a prepared biological mixture, not raw sludge or rumen fluid.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "The existing Sludge_fluid owner spans source-described liquid material from sludge. Its MICRO0000521 exact target asserts municipal origin, while DSMZ119/JCM872 specify anaerobic-digester sludge without that origin. TOGO M2596 separately identifies Ithaca wastewater sludge and its own clarification process. Reuse this existing generic material owner with a local registry identity rather than duplicate it or force municipal origin on every source. The DSMZ119/JCM872 yeast-incubated supernatant is a distinct supplied preparation; the M2596 input and further SS preparation must retain their own source-qualified processing and must not receive the119 formula.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
    "scope_note": "Binding original complete-payload scientific assessments plus actual immutable successor reviews; source-case acceptance alone is not used as owner approval. Historical open findings remain superseded only by separately bound actual corrections."
