        "reasoning": "ATCC 1190/1191 and JCM 221 list the same thirteen non-water input names and amounts, including NTA and cobalt nitrate hexahydrate. ATCC explicitly specifies MnSO4 monohydrate and anhydrous calcium chloride, alum and selenite; JCM uses variable manganese hydration and omits those other hydration qualifiers. Omitted qualifiers do not establish anhydrous identity or a different formulation. Preserve the source-specific fields without reconciling them by assumption. The source-qualified identifiers remain conditional historical proposal handles pending #1237; no winning owner, merge or simultaneous installation as distinct substances is approved. Existing Modified_Wolfes_Minerals has a different documented input list and is a separate comparison dependency. All inherited holds remain.",
