        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "MediaDive 442 leaves the Polypeptone supplier unspecified. BD's composite digest and Wako's casein-only Hipolypepton support retaining the three Hipolypepton alias withdrawals. Remaining Japanese/BD product selection and occurrence allocation remain unresolved. Supplement: the Polypeptone owner fragment retains all original Hipolypepton exclusions and now withdraws the two unsupported globally resolving Nihon Polypepton aliases as provenance-only source labels. Historical primary sources support a casein-derived Nihon product family, not pure final casein or an exact recipe-vintage/SKU bridge; current JCM181 names Hipolypepton (FUJIFILM Wako), so older Nihon labels cannot be globally reconciled by a renamed recipe alone. MediaDive442 still provides no supplier. POLYPEPTONE-001 final grounding is OPEN: the supported FOODON broader relation and the MICRO0000179 exact BD-blend candidate require coordinator selection of the coupled owner/product scope. Feasible source-supported BD curation may proceed separately while ambiguous routes remain held. No assigned case, raw label, occurrence, quantity, source hold or owner/release admission is changed by this supplement.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "Full final materials reassessment, case 160: MediaDive 442 leaves the Polypeptone supplier unspecified. BD's composite digest and Wako's casein-only Hipolypepton support retaining the three Hipolypepton alias withdrawals. Remaining Japanese/BD product selection and occurrence allocation remain unresolved. Supplement: the Polypeptone owner fragment retains all original Hipolypepton exclusions and now withdraws the two unsupported globally resolving Nihon Polypepton aliases as provenance-only source labels. Historical primary sources support a casein-derived Nihon product family, not pure final casein or an exact recipe-vintage/SKU bridge; current JCM181 names Hipolypepton (FUJIFILM Wako), so older Nihon labels cannot be globally reconciled by a renamed recipe alone. MediaDive442 still provides no supplier. POLYPEPTONE-001 final grounding is OPEN: the supported FOODON broader relation and the MICRO0000179 exact BD-blend candidate require coordinator selection of the coupled owner/product scope. Feasible source-supported BD curation may proceed separately while ambiguous routes remain held. No assigned case, raw label, occurrence, quantity, source hold or owner/release admission is changed by this supplement.",
