          "row_sha256": "20f2b7cb20ac80e7cd0097bd4e2dfccb272150a06775ce697d52a2ccbfc2a6e3"
        },
        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "The source label explicitly names D-pantothenate hemicalcium, which is compatible with theD-calcium pantothenate identityCHEBI:31345 rather thanDL salt or free pantothenic acid. The hemicalcium wording expresses the calcium:pantothenate stoichiometry and does not by itself assert a hydrate. The shared owner has erroneousDL and capsaicin-related aliases that this case cannot validate. A single corrected A-P-CALCIUM-D payload now carries the exact source label; this resolves the local proposal-writing dependency while preserving the P5 primary ingredient-table coverage gap.",
        "missing_requirement": "The isolated A-P-CALCIUM-D payload now corrects the baseline unsafe DL/capsaicin aliases and carries this exact D-hemicalcium raw label. Primary MediaDiveP5 currently returns medium metadata only, so recipe-level confirmation of this ingredient remains missing. Retain the P5 source-release hold and require independent native changed-owner/source review; the concrete alias proposal does not establish unpublished source context.",
        "applicability": "Applies to the nutrient-component occurrence of MediaDiveP5 RS medium; it is a vitamin constituent rather than the whole nutrient mixture. Research-a is correcting the sharedD-salt owner. Shared isolated proposal A-P-CALCIUM-D applies only to the substance/formulation established by this case; it does not approve source-case, owner or export release.",
        "source_observations": null
      },
