        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "Complete primary tables distinguish NBRC1020/824 (shared NTA/KOH stock, separate Se/W supplement) from NBRC1308. Independent comparison now shows that NBRC1308 and NBRC1356 have the same13 specified solutes,1L water input, NTA→NaOH pH6.5→minerals and stated finalpH7.0 preparation. Two uninstalled identities are therefore replaced by one reconciled nominal formulation proposal. RecipeIDs, footnotes and metadata differences do not establish another substance.",
        "missing_requirement": "NaOH quantity, form and concentration remain unspecified; 1 L distilled water is an input, not an asserted final volume. The final pH7.0 statement is a condition and does not establish another titration or additional reagent. Source membership is complete relative to the full cited preparation. Retain source-specific dose/processing, all existing source/owner/export holds, and the distinction between nominal input identity and post-processing chemical endpoints.",
        "applicability": "All three original occurrences remain. Only CultureMech:007471 ingredients/8, source nbrc.medium:1308, occurrence CM_OCC:e689137127cd84bead1063ab24e931745a4a44fb673a953471ea3ab33e3a3df5 uses the reconciled stock (1ml, autoclaved with receiving medium underN2/CO2 80/20). CultureMech:007450 ingredients/8 and CultureMech:007496 ingredients/7 remain exclusively A-P-NBRC1020-824-TRACE. Raw Trace element solution** is occurrence-local. No source file basename is used to infer the NBRC accession.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
