        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "The three NBRC recipes1226,335 and392 define different trace-element solutions:1226 uses a high-NTA iron(III) formulation,335 uses a tartrate-based stock, and392 uses a lower-NTA magnesium-rich stock. Their shared starred label is a local table reference, not a substance identity. The335 source also prints H3BO4, which requires source clarification before chemical normalization. Separate exact payloads now capture NBRC1226 and392 for their own occurrence IDs. The NBRC335 occurrence remains unresolved because its primary boron formula is H3BO4; no global synonym or formulation-equivalence claim is made.",
        "missing_requirement": "Obtain a primary NBRC335 correction identifying the H3BO4 reagent and its supplied form before proposing that separate stock. Apply1226/392 proposals only to their enumerated occurrence IDs; no globally resolving Trace element solution* alias.",
        "applicability": "All three frozen occurrences are retained. B-P-NBRC1226-TRACE applies only to CultureMech:007465/nbrc.medium:1226; B-P-NBRC392-TRACE only to CultureMech:007492/nbrc.medium:392. CultureMech:007488/nbrc.medium:335 remains unresolved and is excluded from both proposals. Filename number offsets do not change the embedded source identifiers.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
