        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "NBRC1257 and1321 print the same trace-element stock: acidified iron(II) sulfate heptahydrate plus the other specified trace constituents and water. The two frozen filenames have shifted numbers, so the embedded NBRC identifiers and live compositions, not filenames alone, establish equivalence. This supports one NBRC-qualified stock record. Amounts are preserved as batch inputs because12.5 ml HCl plus987 ml water is not an explicit volumetric make-up to1 L.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "Both occurrences are the starred Trace element mixture of NBRC1257/1321; each source doses1 ml into the parent medium. Generic star labels remain in evidence/notes instead of a global resolving synonym. W06-IR-002 correction: the generic/providerless stock labels are retained exactly as nonresolving REJECTED_LABEL provenance. Routing remains limited to the explicit source recipe/formulation and occurrence partitions already stated here; qualified stock names do not clear source, dose, owner or export holds.",
        "source_observations": null
      },
      {
        "worker_slot": 6,
