          "row_sha256": "adac92181936ead43c27e362b6bec0a14401ceeeb299799b07dff0d70a7d6b62"
        },
        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "JCM439 defines a trace-element stock containing25%HCl, FeSO4 heptahydrate and other metal salts. Its acid/iron composition distinguishes it from the separate187 trace-element formulation. Direct table comparison also matches the NBRC1257/1321 stock proposed by research-b: FeSO4·7H2O2.1g equals2100mg and every other input, acid qualification and water amount agrees. A single shared stock proposal retains this exact numbered pointer as REJECTED_LABEL, with occurrence-specific routing rather than a globally resolving alias.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "All four JCM1363/1364/1400/1444 occurrences explicitly reference439, so the source recipe can be shared across those occurrences only. Shared isolated proposal B-P-NBRC1257-1321 applies only to the substance/formulation established by this case; it does not approve source-case, owner or export release. W06-IR-002 correction: the generic/providerless stock labels are retained exactly as nonresolving REJECTED_LABEL provenance. Routing remains limited to the explicit source recipe/formulation and occurrence partitions already stated here; qualified stock names do not clear source, dose, owner or export holds.",
