        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "JCM1009,825 and837 refer their Trace vitamins component to JCM197, a ten-vitamin stock. TOGO3181 instead explicitly defines biotin0.1 g, p-aminobenzoic acid1 g and thiamine1 g per litre for Rhodospirillaceae medium. This generic-label case therefore has at least two real formulations and cannot resolve globally to JCM197. A current-source-specific RM vitamin stock is now proposed from the mutually consistent narrative and component table. The other three occurrences explicitly reference JCM197 and may link to that existing proposed formulation only by occurrence scope.",
        "missing_requirement": "Apply exact occurrence scopes: RM is the three-vitamin stock; the other three occurrences use JCM197. Any future thiamine salt/hydrate or biotin stereochemistry mapping requires reagent evidence; historical-paper equivalence is not asserted.",
        "applicability": "B-P-TOGO3181-RM-VITAMINS applies only to CultureMech:009631 (RM). CultureMech:007583,013726 and013742 link to JCM197 by the source-defined references; they are explicitly excluded from the RM stock. A generic Trace vitamins synonym on either stock is prohibited. Shared C-P-JCM197 applies ONLY to the three integration_occurrence_ids, excluding the distinct RM stock occurrence. No global Trace vitamins alias. W06-IR-002 correction: the generic/providerless stock labels are retained exactly as nonresolving REJECTED_LABEL provenance. Routing remains limited to the explicit source recipe/formulation and occurrence partitions already stated here; qualified stock names do not clear source, dose, owner or export holds.",
