          "selector": "/90",
          "row_sha256": "313bf74b5d2609fbac0e3905605cb1ad60568ed22f682399f099f2f410719810"
        },
        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "DSMZ29 prints Yeast extrakt; DSMZ40 explicitly follows29 with addedNaCl. This is a direct orthographic source spelling of yeast extract, with no fresh-cell, stock-strength or specialproduct qualifier. FOODON:03315426 and the existingYeast_Extract owner match the ingredient class.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "BothTOGO2258 and2595 occurrences share the source spelling through the29/40 recipe relationship. The proposal adds that raw spelling without changing product composition or occurrence statistics.",
        "source_observations": null
      },
      {
        "worker_slot": 6,
        "binding": {
          "path": "/Users/marcin/Documents/VIMSS/ontology/Mechs/MediaIngredientMech/.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/integration/final-campaign-planning-v1/observed-inputs-v1/snapshot/w06/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-06/successor-v5/decisions.json",
          "sha256": "e626c5147747389c1f1125a22d9b09698700b3e5b4f7bc83b42964c9b47ba54a",
          "selector": "/107",
          "row_sha256": "ec59015125269681ba18d8be1fe69d3d25a23efdb755e5fe85724b6e61fc4bd0"
        },
        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "NBRC1140 prints Yeast extaract with glucose and agar, establishing a spelling error in generic yeast extract. FOODON03315426 is yeast extract and matches the existing owner’s identity. No tissue-culture or autolysate product qualifier occurs.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "The single GYA-medium ingredient at2.5g is an ordinary extract spelling variant. Add RAW_TEXT with source provenance; this does not endorse every historical branded synonym or role on the owner. Shared isolated proposal B-P-Yeast_Extract applies only to the substance/formulation established by this case; it does not approve source-case, owner or export release.",
        "source_observations": null
      },
      {
        "worker_slot": 6,
        "binding": {
          "path": "/Users/marcin/Documents/VIMSS/ontology/Mechs/MediaIngredientMech/.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/integration/final-campaign-planning-v1/observed-inputs-v1/snapshot/w06/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-06/successor-v5/decisions.json",
          "sha256": "e626c5147747389c1f1125a22d9b09698700b3e5b4f7bc83b42964c9b47ba54a",
          "selector": "/144",
          "row_sha256": "7c36a97bb0cc0ee08416501406e56b0eff854dd5e699ed0f774b8f0c75bad35a"
        },
        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "The lowercase yeast extaract in the Desulfobulbus freshwater-medium source is a transposed-letter spelling of yeast extract. The linked DSMZ194 formulation and FOODON03315426 support the generic extract identity; no product fraction or stock percentage is present.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "The one TOGO2529 occurrence is covered by the same bounded typo proposal as case107. It does not confer whole-owner publication approval. Shared isolated proposal B-P-Yeast_Extract applies only to the substance/formulation established by this case; it does not approve source-case, owner or export release.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
