        },
        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "TC Yeastolate is a BD-Difco tissue-culture yeast preparation. JCM896 explicitly names it, and the primary insect-cell yeastolate-fractionation paper identifies Difco TC Yeastolate catalogue255772. Neither source equates the preparation to generic yeast extract or to the separately prepared2% autoclaved Yeastolate owner. A bounded BD-Difco TC product-family owner is now proposed. Exact255772 applies to the two catalogue-qualified recipe occurrences and the primary paper; JCM896 remains catalogue-unspecified within the stated TC manufacturer product name. No manufacturing-lot equivalence or post-processing identity is asserted.",
        "missing_requirement": "Concrete source-qualified complex-preparation proposal is now supplied. Molecular composition, cross-product equivalence and source-release approval remain unasserted.",
        "applicability": "Both occurrences are the same JCM896 ingredient. One frozen record preserves1g source amount and the corrected record1.71233g/L for584ml final medium; the identity decision does not undo that arithmetic.",
        "source_observations": null
      },
      {
        "worker_slot": 6,
        "binding": {
          "path": "/Users/marcin/Documents/VIMSS/ontology/Mechs/MediaIngredientMech/.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/integration/final-campaign-planning-v1/observed-inputs-v1/snapshot/w06/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-06/successor-v5/decisions.json",
          "sha256": "e626c5147747389c1f1125a22d9b09698700b3e5b4f7bc83b42964c9b47ba54a",
          "selector": "/127",
          "row_sha256": "4437529d2ab782608e34098bbc1f20fb622ba830546819a992f93103ad8bc940"
        },
        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "The catalogue255772 label identifies TC Yeastolate as the material used to prepare separate2% and10% solutions. The primary insect-cell yeastolate-fractionation paper identifies that Difco catalogue but describes ultrafiltration as subsequent processing, not an intrinsic property of every TC product. A bounded BD-Difco TC product-family owner is now proposed. Exact255772 applies to the two catalogue-qualified recipe occurrences and the primary paper; JCM896 remains catalogue-unspecified within the stated TC manufacturer product name. No manufacturing-lot equivalence or post-processing identity is asserted.",
        "missing_requirement": "Concrete source-qualified complex-preparation proposal is now supplied. Molecular composition, cross-product equivalence and source-release approval remain unasserted.",
        "applicability": "Both occurrences are components inside solution recipes. They must not be identified with the whole2% autoclaved stock or stripped to generic yeast extract; the percentages belong to preparations containing the product.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
    "scope_note": "Binding original complete-payload scientific assessments plus actual immutable successor reviews; source-case acceptance alone is not used as owner approval. Historical open findings remain superseded only by separately bound actual corrections."
