        "reasoning": "A10% glucose solution is a stock containing glucose and solvent; it is not exact identity with the glucose molecule. The receiving JCM recipes explicitly dispense the solution. Neither10% alone nor a free glucose CHEBI annotation chooses anomer or hydrate. A concrete source-qualified stock proposal now records the established constituents and preparation limits; incomplete analytical or source metadata does not prevent the bounded proposal. Successor v3 removes untranscribed Water from the component assertion; only the explicitly named solute and concentration remain as literal transcription.",
