        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "JCM197 defines ten vitamins and water with explicit amounts. This is a recipe-defined stock, not a generic vitamin chemical class. Existing Wolfe/ATCC-labelled stocks are not automatically identical: their phosphate or pantothenate-form differences preclude a lexical merge. A source-specific local identity is proposed.",
        "missing_requirement": "For receiving-medium verification, recover a successful exact JCM887 or MediaDive J887 source response and preserve the provenance distinction for the three independently corroborated MediaDive alternatives. Reconcile each frozen dose/unit separately before source mapping release; this access gap does not invalidate the separately supported JCM197 stock formula.",
        "applicability": "All 40 frozen occurrences and their exact source references are retained. The separate successful JCM197 source supports the vitamin formulation. JCM receiving requests 737, 876, 887 and 955 returned Nothing found and are access limitations, not positive recipe evidence. Separately captured MediaDive J737/solution4668, J876/solution4863 and J955/solution4977 responses corroborate their exact receiving references to compound1784 labelled Trace vitamins (see Medium No. 197). No successful JCM887 receiving response is asserted. The per-occurrence ledger distinguishes explicit receiving-source bindings from other frozen solution contexts. Frozen dose/unit anomalies remain held and do not alter stock composition. W06-IR-002 correction: the generic/providerless stock labels are retained exactly as nonresolving REJECTED_LABEL provenance. Routing remains limited to the explicit source recipe/formulation and occurrence partitions already stated here; qualified stock names do not clear source, dose, owner or export holds.",
