        "reasoning": "MediaDive1982 retains the explicit JCM284 vitamin-solution reference and star attribute. JCM284 defines the specific vitamin stock, distinct from complete growth media and other trace-vitamin recipes. The proposal replaces the baseline unmapped placeholder with a source-defined formulation registry and literal component quantities; no individual component ontology identity or release approval follows.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "Assigned shard index165; source mediadive.ingredient:1982; exact frozen source_record={\"amount\": 1, \"attribute\": \"*\", \"compound\": \"Trace vitamins solution (see Medium No. 284)\", \"compound_id\": 1982, \"optional\": 0, \"recipe_order\": 17, \"unit\": \"ml\"}. Assessed all 0 embedded downstream holds without changing them. The case digest preserves full nested provenance; KG helper occurrence counts are not measured recipe frequencies. Shared isolated proposal C-P-JCM284 applies only to the substance/formulation established by this case; it does not approve source-case, owner or export release. W06-IR-002 correction: the generic/providerless stock labels are retained exactly as nonresolving REJECTED_LABEL provenance. Routing remains limited to the explicit source recipe/formulation and occurrence partitions already stated here; qualified stock names do not clear source, dose, owner or export holds.",
