        "reasoning": "NBRC1356 has the same complete13-solute/water table and NTA/NaOH preparation as NBRC1308. It does not warrant a distinct whole-stock registry owner merely because its local label has four stars or NaOH metadata/closure were encoded differently. One successor proposal replaces both uninstalled proposals; unknown quantities, water basis and chemical forms remain explicit.",
        "missing_requirement": "NaOH quantity, form and concentration remain unspecified; 1 L distilled water is an input, not an asserted final volume. The final pH7.0 statement is a condition and does not establish another titration or additional reagent. Source membership is complete relative to the full cited preparation. Retain source-specific dose/processing, all existing source/owner/export holds, and the distinction between nominal input identity and post-processing chemical endpoints.",
        "applicability": "The only occurrence, CultureMech:007474 ingredients/6, nbrc.medium:1356, CM_OCC:2c345cfde3bd9095fd0dad8782a6d904e0bf1ef8beb5c12333b78d7916f8cb03, links to the shared nominal formulation. Its10ml filter-sterile concentrated-stock addition inN2-handled medium stays distinct from1308 processing. Raw Trace element solution**** remains local provenance, not a global synonym. Equality of nominal formulation does not assert identical post-processing endpoints.",
        "source_observations": null
