        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "DSMZ600 delegates Hutner salts to DSMZ590. The recovered DSMZ590 recipe is an NTA/mineral mixture with Metals44 and acid/base adjustment, not JCM631 Hunter salts. Its molybdate row is printed (NH4)6MoO7O24 x4H2O, so exact chemical component identity is unresolved even though the nominal recipe is recovered. A nominal source-qualified stock can nevertheless be proposed with the printed unresolved component retained UNMAPPED and a source-relative assertion; no chemically complete decomposition is claimed. Both cited recipes specify approximately7.3g KOH for dissolving NTA; that approximate input is preserved in proposed notes.",
        "missing_requirement": "An authoritative correction or product specification for the malformed molybdate component in DSMZ590 is needed before a chemically exact stock decomposition; preserve all original ingredients and pH adjustments.",
        "applicability": "Applies to exact raw source label \"Hutner's basal salts\" and all 1 frozen occurrence objects, each verified against its complete recipe snapshot hash. DSMZ600 delegates Hutner salts to DSMZ590. The recovered DSMZ590 recipe is an NTA/mineral mixture with Metals44 and acid/base adjustment, not JCM631 Hunter salts. Its molybdate row is printed (NH4)6MoO7O24 x4H2O, so exact chemical component identity is unresolved even though the nominal recipe is recovered. A nominal source-qualified stock can nevertheless be proposed with the printed unresolved component retained UNMAPPED and a source-relative assertion; no chemically complete decomposition is claimed. Both cited recipes specify approximately7.3g KOH for dissolving NTA; that approximate input is preserved in proposed notes.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
