        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "The source attribute is 10% ferric sulfate in 0.01 N sulfuric acid and the row adds 88.8 mL. CAS 10028-22-5 and CHEBI:53438 identify the solute, but the ingredient occurrence is an acidified stock with at least ferric sulfate, sulfuric acid and solvent.",
        "missing_requirement": "Nominal source-qualified stock proposal is concrete; UNKNOWN completeness retains unreported solvent/preparation details. Source-bound integration and complete owner review remain required.",
        "applicability": "Raw Fe2(SO4)3 punctuation can be normalized only at the solute level; exact identity with anhydrous ferric sulfate would discard acid and concentration. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization.",
        "source_observations": null
      },
      {
        "worker_slot": 7,
        "binding": {
