        "applicability": "Applies to exact raw source label '2.5% L-Cysteine . HCl' and all 1 frozen occurrence objects, each verified against its complete recipe snapshot hash. TOGO M2570 adds a 2.5% L-cysteine hydrochloride stock; that percentage-qualified preparation is not the pure CHEBI91247 salt or generic hydrate solution. The flat source has replaced a volume contribution by G_PER_L. The accessible source name does not state the percent basis or hydrate. Proposal ROOT-PROPOSAL-NOMINAL-11 applies only to the listed frozen occurrence context(s). TOGO M2570 specifies a 10 mL aliquot of 2.5% L-cysteine hydrochloride stock prepared under nitrogen and autoclaved before addition. Nitrogen is a preparation atmosphere, not an asserted bulk solute. Solvent, percentage basis and reagent hydrate are unreported; L stereochemistry and hydrochloride are explicit. The frozen G_PER_L quantity is preserved as a source normalization conflict, not used as stock composition.",
