        "applicability": "Applies to exact raw source label 'lactic acid' and all 1 frozen occurrence objects, each verified against its complete recipe snapshot hash. JCM87 actually specifies a 20% lactic-acid titrant as one alternative to hydrochloric acid, used to reach pH5.6. The frozen unqualified label omits the stock strength and alternative-use condition. Do not map this whole source occurrence to a pure lactic-acid enantiomer. Proposal ROOT-PROPOSAL-NOMINAL-23 applies only to the listed frozen occurrence context(s). JCM 87 permits 20% lactic acid OR 1 N to 6 N HCl to adjust the final medium to pH 5.6. This proposal denotes only the lactic acid stock alternative. HCl is not a constituent of it, and pH 5.6 is not the stock pH. Percentage basis, solvent and acid stereochemistry are unreported; the amount is determined by the final-medium pH endpoint.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
