        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "DSMZ 1740 explicitly expands Titriplex 1 as nitrilotriacetic acid. Merck Titriplex I 108416 SDS identifies CAS 139-13-9, agreeing with the source acid formula and mass and CHEBI:44557. Potassium hydroxide is added separately during preparation and is not the supplied substance.",
        "missing_requirement": "Coordinate duplicate-owner reconciliation and existing acid-owner payload defects; the alias proposal alone does not retire Titriplex1.yaml or release unrelated aliases.",
        "applicability": "For source 1590 the trade name is supported as NTA acid, not EDTA or trisodium NTA; the proposed raw alias is added to the already existing acid owner while the unmapped duplicate remains an explicit integration reconciliation. Complete frozen raw record, downstream holds and owner review rows remain bound by the case digest; this decision is not a hold-removal authorization.",
        "source_observations": null
