        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "Exact raw KH2PO4 is already a resolving synonym/preferred label on the live CHEBI:63036 owner; the calcium-sulfate appearance is rejected-label provenance only. No duplicate or additional same-spelling alias would change the evidence or fix an actual gap. Independent complete-owner alias review found a narrow supported repair: Independent review IF1201-R2: preserve the original text and source provenance while changing three unsafe maintained identity aliases to REJECTED_LABEL. The fragment (dibasic) does not identify monobasic potassium dihydrogen phosphate. KH2PO4 (0.4 g/l) and KH2PO4 (7% w/v) encode concentration context or a preparation, not an exact pure-salt identity. This is an owner-alias correction; no claim is made that the standalone (dibasic) fragment currently resolves in a native consumer. Primary identity, chemistry, roles, counts and source holds remain unchanged. The separate issue 811 successor also rejects the two named unsupported formula/family aliases on this owner while retaining prior source and stock-label repairs.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "Applies only to source mediadive case 'mediadive.ingredient:11', label 'KH2PO4', raw label 'KH2PO4'. Reviewed complete frozen original_kg_entry, raw source_record, candidate owners and every native_review_rows/downstream_holds entry. Empty occurrence_ids reflects queue representation, not absence of observations. Issue-1201 reassessment rechecked this exact case and current unchanged owner bytes. No additional alias for the source-local parsing/instruction token is justified; the separate bounded owner-alias correction listed here remains proposed. This does not approve existing whole-owner roles or lift source holds.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
