        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "MediaDive 736 retains literal Na2Mo4 x 2 H2O without an independently identifying CAS/structure. The exact intended chemical remains unresolved. The complete candidate-owner review supports a concrete alias-family correction without resolving that source identity. Independent owner-wide review extends the existing Na2Mo4 x 2 H2O rejection to ten related literal malformed or form-unspecified formula aliases: ['Na2MoSO4 x 2 H2O', 'NaMoO4 x 2 H2O', 'Na2MoSO4', 'NaMoO4', 'Na2MoO7 x 2 H2O', 'Na2MoO7O4 x 2 H2O', 'Na2MO4.2H2O', 'Na2MoO7・2H2O', 'NaMoO4 · 2H2O', 'NaMoO4.2H2O']. CHEBI:75213 denotes disodium molybdate dihydrate, 2H2O.MoO4.2Na. The listed formulas alter sodium/oxygen counts, introduce sulfur, omit hydrate specificity or omit the molybdenum element spelling. Preserve each exact source string and its original provenance as REJECTED_LABEL; do not infer a corrected chemical for any source occurrence. Historical June 16 merge claims cite Edison/MediaDive/OAK generically but do not provide a source-qualified correction witness that establishes universal alias equivalence. The September backfills preserve KG spellings, not independent formula evidence. Primary identifier, structure, roles, counts and source holds remain unchanged.",
        "missing_requirement": "Retrieve the specific source recipe/supplier underlying MediaDive736 and document Na2MoO4·2H2O correction; retain malformed-formula hold pending that evidence.",
        "applicability": "Applies only to source mediadive case 'mediadive.ingredient:736', label 'Na2Mo4 x 2 H2O', raw label 'Na2Mo4 x 2 H2O'. Reviewed complete frozen original_kg_entry, raw source_record, candidate owners and every native_review_rows/downstream_holds entry. Empty occurrence_ids reflects queue representation, not absence of observations. Issue-1201 reassessment: source-qualified preparation proposals apply only within the explicit proposal scope; all original case labels/digests/occurrence IDs and holds are retained. No generic label-to-stock or source-held chemical exact match is introduced.",
        "source_observations": null
