        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "ATCC 1340 NaOH reagent (4 g/100 ml): ATCC 1340 explicitly defines its N NaOH input as 4 g/100 ml and uses 30 ml in cysteine-sulfide reducing agent. The initial reagent solvent is not specified. This explicit mass/volume definition is confined to CultureMech:009208; the five other bare-N occurrences are not automatically assigned this strength. The direct anchor remains the ATCC 1340 reagent explicitly specified as 4 g NaOH per 100 ml. For NaOH acid-base neutralization this nominal strength is consistent with 1 N; it does not establish identical carrier or full preparation. Chopped-meat protocol occurrences using 1 N are conditional comparisons only. Matching receiving meat recipes establish shared use context, not a distinct NaOH substance. The other bare-N occurrences remain unassigned. Issue 1227 completeness refinement: if1201-new-atcc_1340_naoh_4g_100ml is UNKNOWN relative to its cited source input list. This does not change the case-specific source-form or comparison restrictions.",
