        "applicability": "Applies only to source culturemech case '5% Na2S・9H2O', label '5% Na2S・9H2O', raw label '5% Na2S・9H2O'. Reviewed all 8 frozen component occurrences listed in occurrence_context, including their full-recipe notes and preparation. Concentrations/stock qualifiers remain source-bound. Issue-1201 reassessment: source-qualified preparation proposals apply only within the explicit proposal scope; all original case labels/digests/occurrence IDs and holds are retained. No generic label-to-stock or source-held chemical exact match is introduced. The direct anchor remains ATCC 1942, whose 10 ml stock dose and 0.5 g/L final amount support 5% w/v and whose stock is autoclaved under nitrogen. JCM 1020 and previously linked JCM cases specify 5% nonahydrate stocks but omit the percent basis and/or exact stock atmosphere. These omissions do not establish a different substance. Preserve their autoclaving and source instructions as conditional comparisons; do not transfer the ATCC basis, carrier or gas treatment to them or assert exact shared preparation.",
