        "reasoning": "The frozen exact raw source row explicitly defines a thiosulfate stock: 5.0 g in 100 ml H2O, dosed 10 ml. Live ingredient 552 still conflicts among bare formula, pentahydrate CAS/formula and PEG-related ChEBI/mass. A bounded source preparation can retain an UNMAPPED thiosulfate-form component; pure anhydrous/hydrate assignment remains blocked. MediaDive 552 source thiosulfate preparation (5 g in 100 ml water): The exact frozen MediaDive 552 source row specifies 5.0 g Na2S2O3 in 100 ml H2O, dosed as 10 ml. This is a preparation recipe, not an anhydrous solid. Conflicting source CAS/formula/ChEBI fields leave the supplied thiosulfate form UNMAPPED. Water grade, final solution volume and any sterilization are unspecified. The original row is the recipe witness; the live ingredient page confirms identifier conflict, not the stock recipe. Issue 1227 completeness refinement: if1201-new-mediadive_552_thiosulfate_5g_100ml is COMPLETE relative to its cited source input list. This does not change the case-specific source-form or comparison restrictions.",
