        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "ChEBI:100147 establishes nalidixic acid as distinct from its sodium salt. Readable NBRC1301 confirms the named acid in a 30 mg/ml stock. The separate NBRC1314 occurrence retains its frozen label and 100 mg/ml transcription, but exact primary applicability is held after unsuccessful NBRC1314 and TOGO M2023 reads; the normalized note does not substitute for the unread source.",
        "missing_requirement": "Readable exact NBRC1314 or TOGO M2023 primary composition is required to verify that occurrence and its 100 mg/ml stock claim. This does not block the independently supported NBRC1301 acid candidate.",
        "applicability": "CM_OCC:0c4b4cf6bb41a8f450de7de792fc7f12e5c998b15757a5cc8cbf8732c22a566a (NBRC1301) is supported by the readable primary table and separate-filtration instruction. CM_OCC:9b9a89f81c52463d464c370ab10bd2fe099e86ab4d2b17ceab5073aaf22c3cdd (NBRC1314 / TOGO M2023) is source-held and unverified. Both IDs and frozen doses remain; neither whole stock is equated to the acid molecule.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
