        "reasoning": "The source explicitly specifies DL-asparagine with one water. Wako identifies DL-asparagine monohydrate as CAS 69833-18-7. TCI uses 3130-87-8 for a hydrate product, but that number also appears on generic asparagine records; it is not copied. A distinct CAS 69833-18-7 owner retains a broad relation to CHEBI:22653 asparagine. The narrower supplied form uses NARROW_MATCH, which emits skos:broadMatch to the ontology parent; this is not exact identity.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "MediaDive1128 supplies the DL and hydration descriptors. Its derived molarity uses an anhydrous mass and does not override the raw 0.8 g reagent identity. Local ChEBI/NCIT and current OLS CAS searches found no exact term. NCIT:C87433 is excluded because its L synonym and CAS 5794-13-8 identify the L hydrate. The existing rejected hydrate alias remains unchanged.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
    "scope_note": "Binding original complete-payload scientific assessments plus actual immutable successor reviews; source-case acceptance alone is not used as owner approval. Historical open findings remain superseded only by separately bound actual corrections."
  },
