        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "The existing owner identifies ferric pyrophosphate by CHEBI:132767, CAS10058-44-3, structure and accepted synonyms, but uses the malformed Fe4(PO4)2 string as its preferred label. Correct the preferred label and retain the old string as rejected provenance. This repair does not establish what the malformed source occurrence intended.",
        "missing_requirement": "The original reagent label or recipe must establish the chemical intended by Fe4(PO4)2. The inherited CAS and derived molarity follow the current mapping and are not independent evidence for correcting the source occurrence.",
        "applicability": "The frozen MediaDive583 record and current primary cross-reference were inspected. CHEBI defines Fe(III) and diphosphate in a 4:3 ratio; its formula is not Fe4(PO4)2. The source label therefore remains unresolved and its native WITHHOLD is preserved even after the owner naming repair.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
