        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "The three FEBA recipes use unqualified R2A at one-fold strength in liquid outgrowth media. MICRO:0000541 supplies the named R2A-medium concept, while MICRO:0000543 separately denotes R2A agar. A generic named-medium record can preserve this source sense without inventing a supplier or formula.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "All three complete FEBA/CultureBotHT records were inspected. The owner denotes the named base only, not their kanamycin, lactate, Tween or cycloheximide supplements. A DAIGO R2A-broth proposal in worker03 is a product-qualified contrast and is not silently treated as the FEBA product. The six names in the liquid MICRO definition establish neither closure nor concrete omitted inputs, so completeness is UNKNOWN. Definition-level pyruvate is CHEBI:15361; no sodium counterion, quantitative salt recipe or agar-formula inference is added.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
    "scope_note": "Binding original complete-payload scientific assessments plus actual immutable successor reviews; source-case acceptance alone is not used as owner approval. Historical open findings remain superseded only by separately bound actual corrections."
