        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "The full Denger2010 methods identify 10 mM racemic sulfolactate and explicitly cite the Roy2003 synthesis. Roy identifies the synthesized material as sodium sulfolactate. The chain supports a source-defined racemic sodium-sulfolactate preparation; sodium stoichiometry, hydration and isolated-product purity remain unspecified. The narrower supplied form uses NARROW_MATCH, which emits skos:broadMatch to the ontology parent; this is not exact identity.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "MEDIADB:16/CultureMech:015430 cites this exact paper and matches its DSM3043 organism and 10 mM carbon substrate. This evidence does not apply to other unqualified sulfolactate occurrences or identify a single enantiomer. The registry preparation is distinct from the neutral generic acid and from R/S-specific ontology terms.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
    "scope_note": "Binding original complete-payload scientific assessments plus actual immutable successor reviews; source-case acceptance alone is not used as owner approval. Historical open findings remain superseded only by separately bound actual corrections."
