        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "The current owner mixes concentration labels and an L-specific label into the alias channel of sodium lactate. Retype the 1 M stock, 1% stock and L-only label as rejected provenance, retaining their original text and source. The DL salt name and existing identifier remain unchanged; this repairs concrete alias defects without approving the withheld row.",
        "missing_requirement": "Source-row release still requires the content-bound native workflow; this proposal does not certify the existing provisional nutritional role or change the inherited hold.",
        "applicability": "Sigma71720 verifies the DL salt at CAS72-17-3; CHEBI:75228 has an unspecified structure, while CHEBI:232798 explicitly identifies sodium L-lactate. MediaDive943 supplies no stock concentration. Its DL name does not justify exporting either concentration label or the L-only synonym. Existing nutritional-role uncertainty and the native hold are preserved.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
