        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "Primary product evidence identifies Soytone as an enzymatic soybean digest. Record that evidence and the exact scope of the four-member family on the active representative, without treating generic soy peptone, Soytone and every Phytone product as a reviewed exact identity. Three active owners share a broad vegetable-hydrolysate identifier; Bacto_Soytone remains rejected.",
        "missing_requirement": "The existing generic family aggregates multiple source labels and products. Exact product-equivalence or a merge requires the occurrence-level source allocation and the historical product/process specifications; the copied family totals cannot establish those facts.",
        "applicability": "MediaDive667 and MediaDive102 use Soytone and Bacto Soytone respectively. The Thermo/BD product evidence supports soybean-digest material, but does not allocate the shared 1089/833 occurrence totals to catalog products. Soy_Peptone, Soya_Pepton and Soya_Peptone were read in full, along with rejected Bacto_Soytone. Their existing identities, aliases, counts and holds are preserved; this is a bounded provenance proposal, not a completed family merge or product-equivalence approval.",
        "source_observations": null
      },
