        "reasoning": "MICRO:0000113 explicitly includes Trypticase soy broth and describes the standard BBL formulation: casein digest, soybean digest, dextrose, NaCl and dipotassium phosphate. Promote the existing generic Trypticase-soy-broth owner, retaining its history and counts. The NBRC source uses 30 g of this base with agar supplied separately. The actual lookup grade is SYNONYM_MATCH: Trypticase soy broth is an exact synonym of canonical tryptic soy broth, preserving own-identifier exact identity.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "Both NBRC957 and NBRC1045 occurrences have the 30 g base and separate agar/extra NaCl. The generic broth formulation is now supported by the MICRO definition and independent FAO compendium. Their completed agar-plus-salt media are not the same whole formulation. The abbreviated Trypticase Soy (BBL) label remains source-local; no catalog or lot is inferred.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
