        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "TOGO M2313 names mannan from Saccharomyces cerevisiae as one alternative carbon material. The existing CAS9036-88-8 owner wrongly uses an organism parent NCIT:C14271 and auto-derived PubChem870 chemistry. Fresh NCIT identifies a fungus species; PubChem870 is amylotetraose/alpha-1,4-tetraglucose, whereas the supplier COA identifies yeast mannan CAS9036-88-8. CHEBI28808 is a broader mannan category, not the exact source-qualified product.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "Reviewed this exact case 'mannan (Saccharomyces cerevisiae)', its 1 frozen occurrence(s), and each enclosing recipe at the listed component/stock path. Primary evidence is attached only for the source recipes, definitions and processing contrasts relevant to this case. Propose preserving the material CAS and source qualifier, replacing the organism parent by broadMatch to mannan, and withdrawing the unrelated oligoglucan formula/structure/CID; no supplier product or role is assigned to the recipe.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
    "scope_note": "Binding original complete-payload scientific assessments plus actual immutable successor reviews; source-case acceptance alone is not used as owner approval. Historical open findings remain superseded only by separately bound actual corrections."
