        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "JCM 556 names a 1 M phosphate buffer at pH 7.2 and directs mixing 28 mL of 1 M KH2PO4 with 78 mL of 1 M Na2HPO4 to prepare 100 mL. The 106 mL input sum conflicts with that stated final amount. A source-qualified nominal preparation with its two named stock parts can be represented while retaining the conflict; no amount is corrected and no quantitative recipe is certified. The 28+78 mL versus 100 mL conflict, input-stock solvent/hydration and pH-adjustment details remain unresolved. This prevents normalized quantities and equivalence to another formulation, not recognition of the named source preparation.",
        "missing_requirement": null,
        "applicability": "All 1 full frozen occurrence snapshots and linked captured primary contexts were independently reread for case 123. JCM 556 names a 1 M phosphate buffer at pH 7.2 and directs mixing 28 mL of 1 M KH2PO4 with 78 mL of 1 M Na2HPO4 to prepare 100 mL. The 106 mL input sum conflicts with that stated final amount. A source-qualified nominal preparation with its two named stock parts can be represented while retaining the conflict; no amount is corrected and no quantitative recipe is certified. This association is source-bound; raw generic labels remain nonresolving provenance unless explicitly the spelling-only seawater alias.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
    "scope_note": "Binding original complete-payload scientific assessments plus actual immutable successor reviews; source-case acceptance alone is not used as owner approval. Historical open findings remain superseded only by separately bound actual corrections."
