        "outcome": null,
        "reasoning": "JCM 431 and JCM 899 use nominal 25% HCl in trace-element preparation, respectively 12.5 mL and 5 mL per printed receiving stock. The common nominal acid-reagent boundary is represented without equating the two complete trace-element mixtures. Percent basis, solvent and supplied grade remain unknown. Different receiving-stock addition volumes are not evidence of different acid concentrations. Successor-v3: Literal 25%, 32% and 35% are retained as source specifications, not normalized comparable fractions. The cited sources do not state a common percentage basis, carrier, grade or assay tolerance; the exact same-or-distinct preparation relation is unresolved. TOGO M2305/M2746 explicitly calls its 25% input concentrated, so that qualitative label does not exclude a numerical percentage. If comparable definitions and assay ranges were established, a real strength difference could be assessed; they are not established here. Before co-installing overlapping candidates, the coordinator must choose an explicit common bounded partial-material scope preserving every source context, or obtain comparable preparation/product evidence. No owner merge or arbitrary winner is selected.",
        "missing_requirement": "Bounded named preparation remains supportable. Comparable percentage/product evidence or an explicit common partial-material convention is required before overlap reconciliation/co-installation; not a prerequisite for recording the literal source input.",
        "applicability": "All 2 full frozen occurrence snapshots and linked captured primary contexts were independently reread for case 102. JCM 431 and JCM 899 use nominal 25% HCl in trace-element preparation, respectively 12.5 mL and 5 mL per printed receiving stock. The common nominal acid-reagent boundary is represented without equating the two complete trace-element mixtures. This association is source-bound; raw generic labels remain nonresolving provenance unless explicitly the spelling-only seawater alias. Existing source occurrences only; W02 M2305/M2746 is comparative evidence and does not add its cases or occurrences to this proposal.",
        "source_observations": null
      }
    ],
    "scope_note": "Binding original complete-payload scientific assessments plus actual immutable successor reviews; source-case acceptance alone is not used as owner approval. Historical open findings remain superseded only by separately bound actual corrections."
